---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import Visual from '../components/Visual.astro';import {getCollection} from 'astro:content';
const tools=(await getCollection('tools')).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
---
<Base noindex title="Diagrams & capture guide" description="Permanent explanatory diagrams and optional screenshots or clips of the actual tools.">
<section class="section-shell page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">VISUAL GUIDE / DIAGRAMS AND OPTIONAL CAPTURES</div><h1>Diagrams and capture guide.</h1><p class="lead">These diagrams explain how the tools work and remain part of the documentation. Screenshots and short recordings can add a view of the actual interface. They are optional.</p><div class="notice"><div><strong>For an optional capture, focus on the feature.</strong><p>Keep the relevant symbol, settings and output readable. Use a clean chart and anonymised or demo data. Remove account identifiers and private records. For motion, a short before and after sequence is enough. Do not place a live trade for a recording.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section-shell section-space"><div class="capture-grid">{tools.map(tool=><article id={tool.id} class="capture-item"><div class="eyebrow">{String(tool.data.order).padStart(2,'0')} / {tool.data.group==='indicator'?'INDICATOR':'USERSCRIPT'}</div><h2>{tool.data.name}</h2>{tool.data.diagram?<p>Permanent explanatory diagram. No screenshot required.{tool.id!=="symbol-mapper"&&<><br/><strong>Optional interface capture:</strong> {tool.data.capture}</>}</p>:<p><strong>Suggested file:</strong> <code>{tool.id}.webp</code>, or <code>{tool.id}.mp4</code> when an interaction needs motion. Provide a wide desktop crop and a closer feature crop for phone layouts.</p>}<a href={`/tools/${tool.id}/#example`}>See this example on the tool page ↗</a><Visual kind={tool.data.visual} diagram={tool.data.diagram} capture={tool.data.capture}/></article>)}</div></section>
</Base>
